From 26f9d4098462d862eca468673f4f1c7028597eb3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jerrell Niu <jerrell@ilovedigital.com.au>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 00:32:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Step the page gutter and widen the content column
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

.container-wide was mx-auto max-w-content px-6. On a viewport near the
content width that left a 24px gutter, so copy and images ran almost to the
edge of the window — visible on /websites at laptop widths.

Gutter now steps rather than jumping at a single breakpoint:
px-6 sm:px-8 md:px-12 lg:px-16 — 24 / 32 / 48 / 64px. Mobile stays at 24px
deliberately; 64px on a 390px screen spends a third of the viewport on empty
margin. max-w-content goes 1200px -> 1320px.

Note on the numbers: max-width is a border-box value, so the padding sits
inside it. A 1320px max-width with a 64px gutter gives a 1192px content
column, not 1320px. That is up from 1152px before. If the intent is a
1320px *column*, the token needs to be 1448px.

Measured on a production build across 11 viewports from 375px to 2560px:
gutter 24 / 24 / 32 / 48 / 48 / 64 / 64 / 64 / 124 / 268 / 684px at
375, 390, 640, 768, 834, 1024, 1280, 1320, 1440, 1728 and 2560. Nothing
falls below 24px, and the layout centres from 1448px up.

One utility, so every section, the nav and the footer move together.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/app/globals.css | 7 ++++++-
 tailwind.config.ts  | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/app/globals.css b/src/app/globals.css
index 69c47d0..b497b6a 100644
--- a/src/app/globals.css
+++ b/src/app/globals.css
@@ -24,8 +24,13 @@
   .section-y {
     @apply py-[60px] md:py-[120px];
   }
+  /* Page gutter, stepped rather than doubled at one breakpoint:
+     24px phones / 32px large phones / 48px tablets / 64px laptops up.
+     Mobile stays at 24px deliberately — a 64px gutter on a 390px screen
+     spends a third of the viewport on empty margin. Above max-w-content
+     the layout centres and the gutters grow past 64px on their own. */
   .container-wide {
-    @apply mx-auto w-full max-w-content px-6;
+    @apply mx-auto w-full max-w-content px-6 sm:px-8 md:px-12 lg:px-16;
   }
   .eyebrow {
     @apply mb-4 inline-block font-body text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-cyan;
diff --git a/tailwind.config.ts b/tailwind.config.ts
index 8a42a92..1215a34 100644
--- a/tailwind.config.ts
+++ b/tailwind.config.ts
@@ -24,7 +24,7 @@ const config: Config = {
         body: ['var(--font-body)', 'system-ui', 'sans-serif'],
       },
       maxWidth: {
-        content: '1200px',
+        content: '1320px',
       },
     },
   },
-- 
2.43.0


