About, Insights and Contact come out of the header and live in the footer
menu. The header is now Work, the Services dropdown with the four pillars,
and the booking CTA.

Nav.tsx had the links hardcoded while content/site.json already carried a
`nav` array that nothing read. Both menus now render from site.json, so the
header is editable as content rather than code — which is what CLAUDE.md
asks for, and what made this a two-file change instead of a hunt.

Insights was missing from the footer entirely; it was only reachable as
"Blog" under Resources. Added to the footer's main column beside About,
Work and Contact.

Verified on a production build at 390, 1280 and 1440: the header renders
Work and Services and nothing else, on desktop and in the mobile menu.

