From 3cbf0d8660705c5b80cc3eeb2d89597101d9a1ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jerrell Niu <jerrell@ilovedigital.com.au>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 00:41:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Add the founder portrait to the home About section and
 /about hero
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replaces the two grey "Founder portrait" / "Photo of Jerrell" placeholders
with the supplied cut-out at public/images/founder/jerrell.webp, 384px on
both pages.

The asset is an 800x800 webp with a real alpha channel — a cut-out with a
dot field behind it, and the dots are near-black (22,43,47). That is why it
goes straight onto the section background rather than inside the gradient
card the placeholders used: on #0C0E13 the dots read as faint texture and
the subject appears to sit on the page, where a bordered card around a
transparent cut-out would look like a sticker in a box.

Kept at its native 1:1 rather than cropped into the old 4:5 boxes. Cropping
a square to 4:5 means cutting 80px off each side, which clips the shoulders.

The source crops mid-torso, so the portrait ended on a straight horizontal
line against the background — obvious on /about at full size. A .portrait-fade
utility masks the bottom 22% to transparent so it dissolves into the section
instead. Defined once in globals.css because Safari still needs the
-webkit-mask-image prefix alongside the standard property.

The path and alt text live in content/pages/home.json and about.json, typed
as optional on the founder block and HeroBlock, so the placeholder still
renders if either is ever removed — the same pattern as the case-study
thumbnails. Alt text is "Jerrell Niu, founder of I Love Digital". The /about
hero is marked priority since it is above the fold; the home portrait is
not.

Verified on a production build at 1440 and 390: both slots render the
optimised image at 384px with transparency intact and the mask applied.

